### 🔹 **Basic Narration Conversion**

1. **He said, "I am going to school."**
   👉 He said that he was going to school.

2. **She said, "I can swim very fast."**
   👉 She said that she could swim very fast.

3. **Ravi said, "I have finished my homework."**
   👉 Ravi said that he had finished his homework.

4. **The teacher said, "Water boils at 100 degrees Celsius."**
   👉 The teacher said that water boils at 100 degrees Celsius. *(Universal truth – no change in tense)*

5. **I said, "I will help you tomorrow."**
   👉 I said that I would help him the next day.

---

### 🔹 **Interrogative Sentences**

6. **She said to me, "Where are you going?"**
   👉 She asked me where I was going.

7. **He said to her, "Do you like coffee?"**
   👉 He asked her if she liked coffee.

8. **They said to the boy, "Why are you late?"**
   👉 They asked the boy why he was late.

9. **The officer said to him, "Have you completed the task?"**
   👉 The officer asked him if he had completed the task.

10. **I said to him, "Did you see the match?"**
    👉 I asked him whether he had seen the match.

---

### 🔹 **Imperative Sentences**

11. **She said to me, "Please help me."**
    👉 She requested me to help her.

12. **He said to his servant, "Bring me a glass of water."**
    👉 He ordered his servant to bring him a glass of water.

13. **The teacher said to the students, "Do your homework."**
    👉 The teacher told the students to do their homework.

14. **The doctor said to the patient, "Take rest."**
    👉 The doctor advised the patient to take rest.

15. **Mother said to the child, "Don’t eat junk food."**
    👉 Mother told the child not to eat junk food.

---

### 🔹 **Exclamatory Sentences**

16. **He said, "What a beautiful flower it is!"**
    👉 He exclaimed that it was a very beautiful flower.

17. **She said, "How lucky I am!"**
    👉 She exclaimed that she was very lucky.

18. **They said, "Hurrah! We have won the match."**
    👉 They exclaimed with joy that they had won the match.

19. **He said, "Alas! He is dead."**
    👉 He exclaimed with sorrow that he was dead.

20. **She said, "Bravo! You have done well."**
    👉 She applauded him saying that he had done well.

---

### 🔹 **Mixed Practice Set**

21. **The boy said, "I am not feeling well today."**
    👉 The boy said that he was not feeling well that day.

22. **She said to me, "Can you lend me your book?"**
    👉 She asked me if I could lend her my book.

23. **He said, "I saw her at the market yesterday."**
    👉 He said that he had seen her at the market the day before.

24. **I said, "I had never seen such a place before."**
    👉 I said that I had never seen such a place before.

25. **Rohan said, "I will meet you at 6 p.m. tomorrow."**
    👉 Rohan said that he would meet me at 6 p.m. the next day.

